{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Parent\n\nEpic `77e3-28e2-31ec-47ec`, deliverable 4. Rescoped by operator decision 2026-11-02 after\nre-measurement collapsed 4 of the original 5 shapes.\n\n## The gap, re-measured on `origin/main` f1fe7c6f587\n\nThe original plan named 5 \"not a behaviour test\" shapes. Measuring each against the live\nrubric `src/rebar/llm/reviewers/code-review-tests.md` (130 lines; antipattern list\n`:22-71`, false-positive guards `:72-112`) leaves exactly one:\n\n| Shape | Status on `origin/main` |\n|---|---|\n| 1. pinning refactor mechanics | already flagged — `change-detector` `:23-26` |\n| 2. pinning re-export identity | already flagged — `change-detector` `:23-26` |\n| 3. **pinning a LOC ceiling** | **not covered — this story** |\n| 4. pinning import shape | already flagged — `change-detector` `:23-26` |\n| 5. re-running a gate script | deliberately BLESSED — Rule-5 `:81-87` and guard (iii) `:88-94` |\n\nShape 5 is not an oversight: guard (iii) explicitly permits greps of command output from an\nexecuted unit when producer liveness is established. Flagging it would contradict rubric text\nwritten on purpose. It is dropped rather than carried.\n\nShape 3 is the one real gap, and it has a standing decision behind it.\n`docs/adr/0058-the-module-size-limit-file-is-the-only-loc-ceiling.md:26-29` (Accepted) decides:\n\"`.github/module-size-limit.txt` is the single authoritative LOC ceiling ... No other test may\nassert an upper LOC bound on a `src/rebar` file, and none may hard-code a ceiling value.\"\n\nNothing detects a violation. `grep -rn 0058 scripts/ .github/workflows/ tests/unit/test_module_size_contract.py`\nreturns nothing on f1fe7c6f587, and the rubric names no LOC shape. The rule is written down\nand unenforced.\n\n**The 5 live violations**, measured on `origin/main` f1fe7c6f587:\n\n- `tests/unit/test_run_span.py:114` — `<= 800`\n- `tests/unit/test_header_delivery.py:302` — `<= 800`\n- `tests/unit/reconciler/state/test_get_rotation.py:394` — `100 <= ... <= 500`\n- `tests/unit/reconciler/state/test_get_rotation.py:395` — `<= 800`\n- `tests/unit/reconciler/state/test_get_rotation.py:396` — `<= 800`\n\nTwo nearby hits are NOT violations and must stay green:\n`tests/unit/workflow/test_completion_prefetch.py:137` (`len(base) + len(out) <= 500`, a token\nbudget) and `tests/unit/test_wall_clock_assert_lint.py:93` (`elapsed_ms <= 500`, a timing\nassertion). Neither bounds a file's line count.\n\n## The change\n\nAdd one antipattern, `loc-ceiling-pinning`, to the existing antipattern list in\n`src/rebar/llm/reviewers/code-review-tests.md` (`:22-71`), and clean the 5 violation sites.\n\nThis edits one file already in the review path and introduces no new mechanism, so the\nmechanism-delta ratchet (`scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py --check`, exit 0 on f1fe7c6f587)\nstays clean. No new config key, gate, flag, or fixture.\n\nThe criterion is already **blocking**, not advisory: `src/rebar/llm/code_review/criteria_routing.json`\n`tests` entry carries `\"default_posture\": \"blocking\"`, `\"blocking_enabled\": true`,\n`\"block_threshold\": 0.54`, flipped by bug obese-dihedral-ermine. The original plan's criterion\nasserting \"it is still advisory\" was factually false and is removed, not weakened.\n\n**The two ADR 0058 exemptions must be preserved in the rubric text**, or the antipattern will\nfire on code the ADR deliberately keeps:\n\n1. The anti-fragmentation **floor** (ADR 0058 `:31-37`): \"never create files < 100 LOC by\n   splitting\" is retained and explicitly not covered by the prohibition. A lower bound is the\n   opposite check, not a duplicate one. `test_get_rotation.py:394`'s `100 <=` half is a floor;\n   only its `<= 500` half violates.\n2. The sanctioned **mirror**, `tests/unit/test_module_size_contract.py`, which reads the limit\n   through `read_limit()` rather than hard-coding it. A test that sources the ceiling from\n   `.github/module-size-limit.txt` is the ADR's prescribed form and must not be flagged.\n\n## Provider neutrality\n\nPer `project.portability`: the change is rubric prose in a Markdown overlay consumed by the\ncode-review gate's Pass-1 runner. It names no vendor, model, or tool-calling syntax, and adds\nno CI-only trigger — the criterion already runs wherever the code-review gate runs. The paired\neval cases live in `src/rebar/llm/eval_specs/code-review-tests.eval.yaml` (29 cases today,\n`model: anthropic:claude-opus-4-8`), whose model pin is the existing calibration corpus's\nproperty and is not changed by this story.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] The `tests` rubric's antipattern list contains a `loc-ceiling-pinning` entry naming the\n      shape (a test asserting an upper bound on a source file's line count, or hard-coding a\n      ceiling value) and citing ADR 0058 as its authority. Verified by reading\n      `src/rebar/llm/reviewers/code-review-tests.md` and by a test asserting the entry is\n      present in the shipped overlay.\n- [ ] The entry states both ADR 0058 exemptions: an anti-fragmentation LOWER bound is not\n      flagged, and a test that reads the ceiling from `.github/module-size-limit.txt` rather\n      than hard-coding it is not flagged. Verified by a test asserting both exemption clauses\n      are present.\n- [ ] RED PROOF: the overlay flags a diff that adds a hard-coded upper LOC bound. The diff is\n      replayed from git history (`git show b91f8f6830c`, which added the now-deleted\n      `tests/unit/test_config_resolver_seam.py`) because all 5 originally named seam-guard\n      modules are deleted from the tree. Verified by a recall case in\n      `src/rebar/llm/eval_specs/code-review-tests.eval.yaml`.\n- [ ] NO-FIRE PROOF: the overlay does not flag (a) a lower-bound-only assertion, (b) a test\n      reading the limit through `read_limit()`, and (c) a non-LOC numeric bound such as a token\n      budget or an elapsed-milliseconds assertion. Verified by three no-fire cases in the same\n      eval spec, so the antipattern is proven scoped.\n- [ ] All 5 live violations are removed or converted to the sanctioned form:\n      `test_run_span.py:114`, `test_header_delivery.py:302`, and\n      `reconciler/state/test_get_rotation.py:394-396`. The `100 <=` floor at `:394` is retained.\n      Verified by `grep -rn '<= *[0-9]\\{3\\}' tests/` over the named files returning no upper\n      LOC bound, and by the full suite staying green.\n- [ ] `tests/unit/workflow/test_completion_prefetch.py:137` and\n      `tests/unit/test_wall_clock_assert_lint.py:93` are unchanged. Verified by the diff, so\n      the cleanup is proven not to over-reach.\n- [ ] `make verify` passes.\n\n## Out of scope\n\n- Changing the criterion's posture or `block_threshold` (already blocking; a threshold change\n  is a separate calibration decision with its own replay evidence).\n- The 4 collapsed shapes above.\n- A CI script or lint rule enforcing ADR 0058 deterministically. The rubric entry is the\n  review-time check; a deterministic detector would be a new mechanism and a separate ticket.","title":"Add a loc-ceiling-pinning antipattern to the code-review tests criterion"}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1793725259982706934,"uuid":"6e9fcdb0-43e6-4403-8cb4-92ed9affd0ff"}